    <string name="faq_add_q">How do I add a subscription?</string>
    <string name="faq_add_a">Tap plus on the Servers tab. You can paste a link, scan a QR code or take the link from the clipboard.</string>
    <string name="faq_add_action">Add</string>
    <string name="faq_client_q">The subscription says this app is not supported</string>
    <string name="faq_client_a">Some services only give servers to their own apps. Open the subscription and set App spoofing to Auto. If that does not help, try another app from the list.</string>
    <string name="faq_client_action">Open subscription</string>
    <string name="faq_update_q">The subscription does not update</string>
    <string name="faq_update_a">Check your internet and that the subscription is still active. If the service limits devices, contact its support. The error text is in the logs.</string>
    <string name="faq_slow_q">Sites do not open or load slowly</string>
    <string name="faq_slow_a">Try another server. Diagnostics will show where the problem is: internet, server or subscription.</string>
    <string name="faq_speed_q">How do I check VPN speed?</string>
    <string name="faq_speed_a">Turn on VPN and run the speed test. It shows download, upload and ping through the selected server.</string>
    <string name="faq_local_q">Local sites work poorly through VPN</string>
    <string name="faq_local_a">Turn on Bypass domestic sites: they will go without VPN, everything else through it.</string>
    <string name="faq_backup_q">How do I move settings to another device?</string>
    <string name="faq_backup_a">Export settings to a file in Tools, then import it in the same place on the new device.</string>
    <string name="faq_bug_q">Found a bug?</string>
    <string name="faq_bug_a">Open the logs, tap Share and send the file to the author on Telegram with a short description.</string>
    <string name="faq_bug_action">Message</string>
